Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?comms:=20JMAP=20batch=204/6=20=E2=80=94=20poll?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20sync=20engine=20(folders,=20messages,=20body,=20operations)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New self-contained JmapSync drives one sync pass per service poll from a single
ServiceSynchronize.monitorAccount hook (replaces the TYPE_JMAP skip guard):
 - folders: Mailbox/get -> upsert EntityFolder (role->type, parent paths)
 - messages: Email/query+get -> EntityMessage, dedup by uidl = JMAP Email.id
   (mirrors the POP uidl pattern; re-poll never duplicates/drops), threadId
   used verbatim, keywords -> seen/flagged/answered, body deferred to a BODY op
 - body: lazy Email/get bodyValues -> message file + setMessageContent
 - operations (batch 6): drain SEEN/FLAG/MOVE/DELETE/BODY -> JmapService.data-plane

Batch 5 (send) is stubbed (JmapSync.onSend) pending EmailSubmission/upload API
confirmation against the built classpath — the submission source 404'd.

Tester: runner build + activate JMAP account (jmap.diegonmarcos.com) -> Inbox +
folders populate; cross-check provider unread vs server STATUS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
